{title: Daughter of Haran}
{subtitle: Genesis 11:29; 11:28; 11:27–31}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 72}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [F/A] | [Gm] [Bbmaj7/F] |
| [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]Terah lived in Ur of the Chal[F/A]deans
[Gm]Father of Abram, Nahor, and [Eb]Haran
Haran [Bb]died in the land of his [F/A]birth
While his [Gm]father Terah was still alive [Eb]on earth
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Bb]Abram and Nahor both took [F/A]wives
Sa[Gm]rai was the name that Abram [Eb]lives
[Bb]Nahor's wife was named Milc[F/A]ah
Daughter of Ha[Gm]ran, born in that [Eb]place
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
She is the daugh[Bb]ter of Haran
Iscah, named [F/A]in the ancient clan
Sister to [Gm]Lot and Milcah
Living in [Eb]Ur, waiting to [Bb]go
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Instrumental}
| [Bb] | [F/A] | [Gm] | [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Bb]Sarai was barren, she [F/A]had no child
[Gm]Terah packed the family for a wild [Eb]ride
[Bb]Took his son Abram, [F/A]grandson Lot
And Sa[Gm]rai, the wife, to go forth [Eb]
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{comment: Instrumental}
| [Bb] | [F/A] | [Gm] | [Eb] |

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Bb]They left Ur of the Chal[F/A]deans behind
[Gm]Heading for Canaan, a land [Eb]to find
[Bb]But when they came to Ha[F/A]ran
They settled [Gm]there, as the story be[Eb]gan
{end_of_bridge}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Remains [F/A]in the text, brief and [Gm]clear
Iscah, [Eb]daughter of Haran, ap[Bb]pears
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
